{
  "_about": [
    "The pinned reconciliation sample for preprod (F1 check 6). PINNED, NOT DRAWN AT RUN TIME:",
    "a check whose population changes between runs cannot tell a fixed divergence from a",
    "different sample, and `git diff` on this file is how a population change becomes visible.",
    "",
    "No randomness anywhere. A shell script cannot draw a reproducible random sample, so both",
    "lists are the union of DETERMINISTIC selectors and are sorted, which means a redraw either",
    "matches this file byte for byte or shows a real change.",
    "",
    "vote_history_dreps (R7) = the 30 DReps with the most vote rows (the interesting tail)",
    "  UNION the 10 most recently registered DReps with at least one vote (the newest cohort,",
    "  which the tail never covers) UNION the worked-example DRep, explicitly, because its 16",
    "  votes are not guaranteed to reach the top 30 and a test asserts it is here UNION one DRep",
    "  that actually re-voted, so R7's superseded-vote path is exercised against live data.",
    "  That last id is the ONE value drawn with a Koios call, and it is an id both sides are then",
    "  compared on -- never a value either side is judged by.",
    "",
    "tally_actions (R6, R9) = every ratified action, every dropped-only action, the 5 treasury",
    "  withdrawals with the largest total, and the 2 oldest bootstrap-era actions: every",
    "  lifecycle shape and the whole withdrawal path.",
    "",
    "Redraw with the commands in docs/superpowers/F1-PROGRESS.md under T-PARITY-4."
  ],
